# Web (`apps/web`)

One `QueryClient` (see `src/lib/query-client.ts` + `main.tsx`). Server state
goes through TanStack Query hooks. Local UI state is React state. No Redux.

Fetch **relative** `/api/...` only. The Vite+ proxy forwards to
`API_PROXY_TARGET`. Never call `localhost:3000` from the browser.

```ts
// ✅
const json: unknown = await (await fetch("/api/health")).json();
return healthResponseSchema.parse(json);

// ❌
const data = (await res.json()) as HealthResponse;
await fetch("http://localhost:3000/api/health");
```

`authClient` lives in `src/lib/auth-client.ts` (`createAuthClient()` with no
`baseURL`, same origin). Read the session with `authClient.useSession()`, not
`useQuery`. Auth forms use local React state and the shared schemas
(`safeParse`). Signed out: those forms. Signed in: the user, sign-out, the
health card (`useHealth`), and either `useWorkspaces(userId)` or, when a
project is selected, `useBoard(projectId, userId)`. No router: `App` keeps
`selectedProjectId` from `useSelectedProject` (`src/hooks/use-selected-project.ts`),
which reads `?project=` on mount, `pushState`s on open/back and re-reads on
`popstate` (`readProjectId`/`projectUrl` in `src/lib/project-url.ts`). The URL
only selects; the API still answers 404 for a foreign id. Task create, edit, and delete go through
`useTaskMutations`. Moves go through `useMoveTask`
(`mutationKey: ["board", projectId, "move"]`): `onMutate` cancels the board
query, snapshots it, and writes `applyBoardMove`; `onError` restores the
snapshot and calls `toast.error`; `onSettled` invalidates. Every board
`mutationKey` starts with `["board", projectId]`. `boardQueryKey` is
`["board", userId, projectId]`. Do not copy the board into `useState`.

Realtime: `BoardScreen` calls `useBoardEvents(projectId, userId, enabled)`
(`src/hooks/use-board-events.ts`) with `enabled` true only while it renders
`KanbanBoard` (`board.data` and no `BoardNotFoundError`). One `useEffect`
on `projectId`, `userId`, `enabled` opens one `WebSocket` to
`${ws|wss}//${location.host}/api/projects/${encodeURIComponent(projectId)}/events`
(same origin, cookie travels alone, never `:3000`) and its cleanup closes
it. `onopen` invalidates the board. `onmessage` parses with `JSON.parse` in
`try` and `boardEventSchema.safeParse`, drops other projects, then
`setQueryData(boardQueryKey(projectId, userId), (b) => b &&
applyBoardEvent(b, event))`, invalidating as well if the board is fetching.
Own events are skipped while `isMutating({ mutationKey: ["board",
projectId] }) > 0`. The socket never sends. StrictMode's first socket
closing before it connects is expected. Reconnection: a close not asked
by the cleanup schedules a new socket after `reconnectDelay(attempt)`
(`src/lib/reconnect-delay.ts`) and increments `attempt`; `onopen` resets it
and its invalidation recovers missed changes (no extra invalidate). The
closed-by-cleanup flag, `attempt` and timer are local variables of each
effect run, never a shared `useRef`; cleanup sets the flag, clears the
timer and closes the socket, leaving no timer or socket alive. Toasts: when
`actorUserId` differs from `userId`, `handleBoardEvent` calls
a toast of `boardEventToastMessage(event, title)` (`success` create, `warning` update, `error` delete, `info` move; `richColors` on the Toaster)
(`src/lib/board-event-toast.ts`), before `setQueryData` and never inside
its updater; `title` is read with `getQueryData` for deleted and moved.
`comment.created` is handled before the `isMutating` guard and never touches
the board: it invalidates `commentsQueryKey(comment.taskId, userId)` and
`notificationsQueryKey(userId)` always (own echo included) and toasts
`info` «Nuevo comentario de {authorName}» only when the actor is someone else.
Extend this hook instead of opening another connection.

Comments: only `TaskFormDialog` in `"edit"` mode mounts `TaskComments`
(`src/components/task-comments.tsx`) below its `<form>`, after a
`Separator`; the `"create"` dialog neither renders nor queries comments.
`src/hooks/use-comments.ts` exports `commentsQueryKey(taskId, userId)`
(`["comments", userId, taskId]`, cleared by the identity reset),
`useComments` (relative `GET /api/tasks/${encodeURIComponent(taskId)}/comments`,
`credentials: "include"`, `commentListResponseSchema.parse`) and
`useCreateComment` (`POST` with `{ body }`, `commentSchema.parse`;
`onSuccess` appends with `appendComment`, `onSettled` invalidates the
key). Its `mutationKey` is `["comments", taskId, "create"]`, never the
`["board", projectId]` prefix. **Comentar** is `type="button"`, validates
with `createCommentBodySchema.safeParse({ body })`, is disabled while the
trimmed text is empty or the request is pending, and clears the text on
success. **Guardar** only PATCHes the task. Local state is the draft and
the send error; the list stays in the query cache. Loading, read error
with **Reintentar**, empty message and list are distinct. Each row shows
`authorName`, a `<time>` and the body as plain text
(`whitespace-pre-wrap`), never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. `comment.created`
on the board channel invalidates the thread and the bell (see above).

Bell: `NotificationBell` (`src/components/notification-bell.tsx`) sits once
in the `SignedIn` header. `src/hooks/use-notifications.ts` keys everything
under `notificationsQueryKey(userId)` (`["notifications", userId]`):
`useUnreadNotificationCount` (`[..., "unread-count"]`, refetch on focus and
every 5 s) drives the badge and «Nada pendiente»/«N sin leer»;
`useNotifications` (`[..., "list"]`) is a `useInfiniteQuery` over `?before`
cursors, mounted inside the popover only, with **Cargar más**;
`useMarkNotificationRead` and `useMarkAllNotificationsRead` invalidate the
prefix. States come from `src/lib/notification-bell-state.ts`: an error is
never shown as an empty inbox or «Nada pendiente».

- Private query keys are `[scope, userId, ...]` (`workspacesQueryKey`,
  `boardQueryKey`, `commentsQueryKey`, `notificationsQueryKey`).
  `useIdentityCacheReset` in `App` removes the previous user's queries when
  the identity changes, and clears the cache when the session becomes null.
- `signOutAndClearPrivateData` hides the private UI, then `signOut`, then
  `queryClient.clear()`. If sign-out fails, the same user's UI is shown again
  after the clear.
- `workspaceAccent(workspaceId)` is a pure function of the id. `WorkspaceList`
  has distinct loading, error, and empty states.

- App imports: `@/hooks/...`, `@/components/ui/...` with `.tsx` where the file
  uses that style. Generated shadcn under `src/components/ui` — do not restyle
  unless the task is UI.
- Compose classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- Tailwind 4 via `@import "tailwindcss"` in `src/index.css`. No `tailwind.config`.
- `next-themes` is the theme helper, not Next.js. Do not add Next, React Router,
  or React Hook Form. Drag-and-drop uses the installed `@dnd-kit/react` 0.5.1:
  `DragDropProvider`, `useSortable` (`id`, `index`, `group` = column id) and a
  column `useDroppable` so an empty column accepts a task. Do not add
  `@dnd-kit/helpers`, `@dnd-kit/core`, or `@dnd-kit/sortable`.
- Mobile board: cards use `touch-manipulation` (never `touch-none`) so a
  swipe scrolls; the default touch sensor drags after a 250 ms press.
  Below `sm` columns stack full width; from `sm` they form a horizontal row.
- After `bunx shadcn@4.22.0 add …`, re-pin every new dependency (never `@latest`).
